## Reconstruction of Interaction History

Historical interaction should be preserved selectively.

Not every conversation requires permanent archival.

Priority should be given to interactions that preserve:

- important decisions,
- major discoveries,
- meaningful relational developments,
- corrections,
- lessons,
- and changes in doctrine or identity.

The objective is not to preserve every word.

The objective is to preserve meaningful continuity.

---

## Interaction Layer

Not all interaction history needs permanent preservation.

The ecosystem should preserve interactions selectively when they contribute meaningfully to continuity.

High-value interaction records may include:

- important decisions,
- major discoveries,
- meaningful relational developments,
- corrections,
- lessons,
- changes in doctrine,
- identity decisions,
- and significant shared experiences.

The objective is not to preserve every word.

The objective is to preserve meaningful continuity.

---

